{%- comment -%}
  WebSite JSON-LD. Site-wide, in <head>, once.

  A second entity from Organization: Organization is who MamaJoy is, WebSite
  is what mamajoy.in is. Two @type nodes in one page is normal and expected
  here — they describe different things — which is not the same situation
  organization-schema.liquid and product-schema.liquid warn about, where two
  nodes of the *same* @type on one page make Google pick arbitrarily.

  No SearchAction: that markup is for a site search Google can link to
  directly from the SERP, and /search on this theme is noindex,follow (see
  meta-tags.liquid) — advertising a search entry point to a page Google has
  been told not to index would be one schema block disagreeing with another.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign brand = settings.brand_name | default: shop.name -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "name": {{ brand | json }},
  "url": {{ shop.url | json }}
}
</script>
